## The pier, early

::bg{location="pier" time="morning"}
::music{playback="start" mood="peaceful" volume="down"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: The tide is out. Boats lie on their sides in the mud like tired dogs.
::actor{character="theo" anchor="right" action="slideInRight"}
::set{run.seen.theo = run.day}
@theo{code="0010" emotion="neutral" as="Boy with the nets"}: You're standing on my nets.
@sol{code="0010"}: Sorry! I'm — Pell's. Her nephew. I'm supposed to find reed?
@theo{code="0020" emotion="surprised" as="Boy with the nets"}: Pell's making a lantern this year? I thought her hands…
@theo{code="0030" emotion="shy" as="Boy with the nets"}: Sorry. That's not mine to say. I'm Theo. Maddox. My dad had the Kittiwake.

<branch id="theoFirst" prompt="Theo keeps coiling rope, not looking at you.">
  <choice id="honest" text="“She asked me to make it for her.”">
    ::set{run.aff.theo += 1}
    @theo{code="0040" emotion="happy"}: Then you'll want the green reed, not the brown. Brown snaps when it's wet.
  </choice>
  <choice id="joke" text="“I'm the hands now. Very qualified hands.”">
    @theo{code="0050" emotion="teasing"}: Qualified. Sure. Come back tomorrow when the reed's dried, qualified hands.
  </choice>
</branch>

::actor{character="theo" action="slideOut"}
@sol{code="0020" mono}: He smells like diesel and cut grass. I don't know why I noticed that.
